  "question": {
    "text": "A single slit of width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is illuminated by a coherent monochromatic light of wavelength <math><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the second and fourth minima in the diffraction pattern at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the slit are at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> respectively from the central maximum, what is the width of the central maximum? (i.e. distance between first minimum on either side of the central maximum)"
  },
